      <main id="main">
        <section>
          <h2>
            <span class="num">Section 1</span>Who we are and what these Terms
            cover
          </h2>
          <p>
            Fifth Wheel is operated by Fifth Wheel Supper Club, LLC, a Georgia
            limited liability company doing business as Fifth Wheel
            (&ldquo;Fifth Wheel,&rdquo; &ldquo;we,&rdquo; &ldquo;us,&rdquo;
            &ldquo;our&rdquo;). These Terms of Service (&ldquo;Terms&rdquo;)
            govern your use of our website, application forms, text messages,
            and the curated dining events we organize (together, the
            &ldquo;Service&rdquo;).
          </p>
          <p>
            Fifth Wheel curates evenings for five verified single guests. A
            single evening moves through three stops in one Atlanta neighborhood
            &mdash; drinks, dinner, and dessert &mdash; and closes with a
            private, anonymous mutual-interest vote. We are the organizer of
            that evening. We are not a restaurant, a bar, a caterer, a
            transportation provider, a matchmaking agency, or a
            background-screening service.
          </p>
          <p>
            By submitting an application, accepting a seat, paying a reservation
            fee, or attending an event, you agree to these Terms. If you do not
            agree, do not use the Service.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2><span class="num">Section 2</span>Eligibility</h2>
          <p>To apply for or attend a Fifth Wheel evening, you must:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Be at least 21 years of age;</li>
            <li>
              Be legally single and not presenting yourself as available under
              false pretenses;
            </li>
            <li>Be able to attend events in the metropolitan Atlanta area;</li>
            <li>
              Complete our identity verification requirements (Section 4);
            </li>
            <li>
              Have never been removed from the Service for a conduct violation;
              and
            </li>
            <li>Maintain one account and one identity on the Service.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            We may verify eligibility at any time and may decline or revoke
            access if we cannot confirm it.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>
            <span class="num">Section 3</span>Application, curation, and seat
            offers
          </h2>
          <p>
            Applying to Fifth Wheel does not reserve a seat and does not
            guarantee placement at any evening. Every table is assembled by a
            human coordinator. There is no algorithm, no queue position, and no
            entitlement to a seat based on the order or timing of your
            application.
          </p>
          <p>
            When a coordinator builds a table you fit, we will send you a
            personal invitation containing the date, neighborhood, approximate
            timing, and a link to confirm and pay. Invitations expire on the
            deadline stated in the invitation. Your seat is reserved only when
            payment is completed.
          </p>

          <h3>Curation criteria</h3>
          <p>
            Coordinators consider stated availability, neighborhood, age band,
            and the conversational balance of the group. We do not guarantee any
            particular composition of the table, any particular number of guests
            you will find compatible, or any particular outcome from the
            evening. Any themed or topical element of an evening is a
            conversation framing only and is never used to determine who may
            attend.
          </p>
          <p>
            We may decline an application, decline to seat you at a specific
            table, or discontinue seating you entirely, at our discretion,
            subject to applicable law. We are not obligated to give reasons.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2><span class="num">Section 4</span>Identity verification</h2>
          <p>
            Verification is the foundation of the format. Every guest at every
            table completes it. Verification may include confirming a mobile
            number by one-time code and confirming a government-issued photo ID
            through our third-party identity verification provider. You agree
            that the information you submit is true and belongs to you.
            Submitting another person&rsquo;s identity documents, an altered
            document, or a photograph of a photograph is grounds for immediate
            and permanent removal without refund.
          </p>
          <div class="callout">
            <p>
              Verification confirms that you are who you say you are. It is
              <strong>not</strong> a criminal background check, a sex-offender
              registry search, an employment or credit check, or a character
              assessment, and you should not treat another guest&rsquo;s
              presence at the table as a representation by us about that
              person&rsquo;s history, intentions, or safety. Section 15 applies.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>
            <span class="num">Section 5</span>Reservation fees and what they
            include
          </h2>
          <h3>Reservation fee</h3>
          <p>
            A confirmed seat costs <strong>$25.00</strong> per person, per
            evening, charged at the time you accept your invitation. Payment is
            processed by our third-party payment processor; we do not store your
            full card details.
          </p>
          <p>
            The reservation fee covers curation, verification, coordination with
            the three venues, and running the evening &mdash; including reserved
            space at each stop and the mechanics of the vote.
          </p>
          <p>
            The reservation fee <strong>does not include food or drink</strong>.
            You are responsible for your own food, beverages, tax, and gratuity
            at each of the three stops, paid directly to each venue. Prices are
            set by the venues, not by us. Bring a form of payment. You are also
            responsible for your own transportation, parking, and any other
            personal costs of attending.
          </p>
          <p>
            Fees are stated in U.S. dollars and are exclusive of any applicable
            taxes, which will be added where required.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>
            <span class="num">Section 6</span>Cancellations, changes, and
            no-shows
          </h2>
          <p>
            A Fifth Wheel evening is built for exactly five people. When one
            guest withdraws late, the coordinator does not simply lose one seat
            &mdash; the table&rsquo;s balance is broken for four other verified
            guests who have already arranged their evening. Our refund terms are
            firm for that reason, and they are the same for everyone.
          </p>

          <h3>If you cancel</h3>
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>When you cancel</th>
                <th>What you receive</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>24 hours or more before start</td>
                <td>Full refund of the reservation fee</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Between 6 and 24 hours before</td>
                <td>50% of the reservation fee refunded</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Less than 6 hours before</td>
                <td>No refund</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>No-show, or arrival after the first stop closes</td>
                <td>No refund</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
          <p>
            If you accept an invitation less than six (6) hours before the
            event, your reservation fee is non-refundable from the moment of
            purchase. This is disclosed again at checkout.
          </p>
          <p>
            Refunds are issued to the original payment method and typically post
            within five to ten business days. Refund tiers are measured against
            the published start time of the first stop, in Eastern Time, and are
            determined by when we receive your cancellation through the link in
            your confirmation.
          </p>

          <h3>Repeated late cancellation</h3>
          <p>
            Two late cancellations or no-shows within a rolling twelve-month
            period may result in removal from future seating. This is not a
            penalty fee; it is a seating decision.
          </p>

          <h3>Emergencies</h3>
          <p>
            We may, at our sole discretion and without setting a precedent, make
            an exception in the case of a genuine emergency. Any such exception
            is a courtesy, not an entitlement, and does not modify these Terms.
          </p>

          <h3>Transfers</h3>
          <p>
            Seats are personal to you and may not be transferred, sold, gifted,
            or given to another person. Every guest at the table must be
            individually verified and individually curated.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>
            <span class="num">Section 7</span>Changes or cancellation by Fifth
            Wheel
          </h2>
          <p>
            We may substitute a venue, adjust timing, or change the running
            order of the evening. Where a change is material, we will notify you
            as far in advance as we reasonably can.
          </p>
          <p>
            If we cancel an evening for any reason &mdash; including a venue
            closure, a table that falls below the minimum number of guests,
            weather, or a safety concern &mdash; you will receive a full refund
            of your reservation fee, or the option to be seated at a future
            evening at no additional cost. That is our entire obligation to you
            in the event of a cancellation by us. We are not responsible for
            your travel, childcare, wardrobe, cancelled plans, or other
            incidental costs.
          </p>
          <p>
            If a guest withdraws close to the event and we cannot replace them,
            we may run the evening with four guests, seat a substitute, or
            cancel. An evening that runs with fewer than five guests is not a
            cancelled evening and does not entitle you to a refund.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2><span class="num">Section 8</span>Conduct at the table</h2>
          <p>
            The format only works because everyone at the table has agreed to
            the same terms. While using the Service and while attending any
            event, you agree that you will not:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              Harass, threaten, demean, or intimidate any guest, host, or venue
              staff member;
            </li>
            <li>
              Make unwanted physical contact, or continue any advance after it
              has been declined;
            </li>
            <li>
              Photograph, film, or record another guest without that
              guest&rsquo;s express permission;
            </li>
            <li>
              Share another guest&rsquo;s name, image, contact details,
              employer, or personal information outside the table;
            </li>
            <li>
              Attend under the influence to the point of disruption, or become
              disruptive during the evening;
            </li>
            <li>
              Use the evening to sell, recruit, solicit investment, promote a
              business, or gather leads;
            </li>
            <li>
              Attend while married, partnered, or otherwise unavailable, without
              disclosing that fact; or
            </li>
            <li>
              Violate any venue&rsquo;s own rules, dress code, or instructions
              from its staff.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            A coordinator or host may end your participation in an evening at
            any time if your conduct warrants it. If you are asked to leave, you
            leave, and no refund is due.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>
            <span class="num">Section 9</span>The vote and mutual interest
          </h2>
          <p>
            At the close of the evening, each guest privately indicates who, if
            anyone, they would like to be introduced to. Votes are anonymous. We
            disclose a vote only where interest is mutual, and only to the two
            guests involved. If no match results, no one is told who voted for
            whom, and nothing is disclosed to the rest of the table.
          </p>
          <p>
            If a match results, we share the two guests&rsquo; first names and
            the contact method each has designated. What happens after that
            introduction is entirely between the two of you and is outside the
            Service.
          </p>
          <p>
            You may decline to vote, and you may withdraw a match before contact
            information is exchanged by telling us before the exchange occurs. A
            match is an introduction, not a commitment, and carries no promise
            about the other person.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>
            <span class="num">Section 10</span>Alcohol and personal
            responsibility
          </h2>
          <p>
            Alcohol may be available for purchase at any of the three stops.
            Fifth Wheel does not sell, serve, supply, or provide alcohol, and no
            alcohol is included in your reservation fee. All alcohol service is
            performed by the licensed venue, subject to its own policies and
            Georgia law.
          </p>
          <p>
            You are solely responsible for your own consumption and for
            arranging safe transportation to and from every stop. Do not drive
            impaired. If you appear intoxicated, a venue may refuse you service
            and we may end your participation in the evening, without refund.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>
            <span class="num">Section 11</span>Allergies, dietary needs, and
            accessibility
          </h2>
          <p>
            Fifth Wheel curates restaurant partners with the goal of offering
            menus that can accommodate a range of dietary preferences, including
            vegetarian, vegan, and gluten-free options. However, menu
            availability, ingredients, preparation methods, and allergen
            practices are determined solely by each venue and may change.
          </p>
          <p>
            You are solely responsible for communicating any food allergy,
            intolerance, dietary restriction, or other food-related requirement
            directly to the restaurant staff at each venue before ordering or
            consuming food or beverages. Fifth Wheel does not communicate
            individual allergy information to venues on your behalf and is not
            responsible for determining whether any menu item or venue is safe
            or appropriate for you.
          </p>
          <p>
            Fifth Wheel does not prepare, handle, or serve food and cannot
            guarantee the accuracy of ingredient information or any
            venue&rsquo;s handling of allergens, cross-contact, food
            preparation, or dietary requests. If you have a food allergy,
            particularly a severe allergy, you should speak directly with venue
            staff before ordering and take any precautions or carry any
            medication appropriate for your needs. You are responsible for
            deciding what you consume.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you have an accessibility requirement that may affect your
            ability to participate in an evening, please tell us when you apply.
            We will make reasonable efforts to select suitable venues and
            experiences, but not every venue or neighborhood can accommodate
            every accessibility need. We may therefore offer you a different
            evening or location.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>
            <span class="num">Section 12</span>Your information and privacy
          </h2>
          <p>
            What you share with us is central to whether this works, and we
            treat it that way. Our
            <a href={withBase("privacy/")}>Privacy Policy</a> describes in full what we
            collect, who receives it, how long we keep it, and the rights you
            have over it. It forms part of these Terms.
          </p>
          <p>
            In summary: venues receive a confirmed party count and nothing else
            about you. Other guests see your first name and selected profile
            elements, and never your contact details unless a mutual match
            results and you choose to share them. Other guests never see your
            votes. We do not sell your personal information.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2><span class="num">Section 13</span>Content you provide</h2>
          <p>
            You keep ownership of the photographs, written answers, and other
            content you submit. You grant us a non-exclusive, royalty-free
            license to use that content for the purpose of operating the Service
            &mdash; showing your profile elements to the other four guests at
            your table, and to our coordinators.
          </p>
          <p>
            We will not use your name, photograph, or words in marketing, on our
            website, or on social media without your separate, express, written
            permission. Permission given for one use is not permission for all
            uses, and you may withdraw it at any time going forward.
          </p>
          <p>
            You are responsible for the accuracy of what you submit. Photographs
            must be recent and must be of you.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>
            <span class="num">Section 14</span>Reporting, suspension, and
            removal
          </h2>
          <p>
            If something happens at a table that concerns you, tell us. Every
            guest is given a direct channel to a coordinator, and a report goes
            to a coordinator only &mdash; never to the guest it concerns, and
            never to the rest of the table.
          </p>
          <p>
            We may suspend or permanently remove any guest at our discretion,
            including while we look into a report. Removal for a conduct
            violation does not entitle you to a refund of any reservation fee
            already paid, including for an evening you have not yet attended.
          </p>
          <p>
            We are not a law-enforcement agency and we do not adjudicate
            disputes between guests.
            <strong
              >If you believe you are in danger, contact emergency services by
              dialing #911.</strong
            >
          </p>

          <h3>Prohibited uses of the Service</h3>
          <p>
            In addition to Section 8, you may not: create an account for anyone
            other than yourself; use the Service on behalf of a business;
            scrape, copy, or reproduce our materials, itineraries, or venue
            lists; attempt to identify other guests through our systems;
            interfere with the operation of our website or messaging; or use the
            Service for any unlawful purpose.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>
            <span class="num">Section 15</span>Assumption of risk, disclaimers,
